WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.550
Ryan Reynolds has always been a fun-loving,
good-looking guy.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.830
But if you compare his early days in Hollywood
to his more recent outing as everyone's favorite

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.889
foulmouthed superhero, you might notice that
he hasn't always had the beefed-up physique

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:13.719
that looks so good in red spandex.

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:17.070
How did this former child actor turn his body
from lean to mean?

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.130
Be warned: there aren't any tricks — just
time, energy, and dedication.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.599
It all began with Blade

00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:26.859
Reynolds' big comic book movie breakthrough
came over a decade ago, when he played vampire

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:30.410
hunter Hannibal King in the 2004 film Blade:
Trinity.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.950
"The trainer before we started the film wanted
to pack on about ten pounds on me and muscle

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.950
up"

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.870
In the three months before filming began,
Reynolds was whipped into good enough shape

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.660
to occupy space in a superhero flick, if not
headline one himself.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.660
The secret?

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.080
Long workouts, heavy weights, and zero cardio
— because believe it or not, before he packed

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.160
on the muscle to play this role, Ryan Reynolds
was kind of a noodle.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.739
Every day is a gym day

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:55.050
Wanna be a superhero?

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.720
Prepare not to slack off… ever.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.640
"Mmmmmaximum effort!"

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.100
Some of the routines Reynolds has to follow
border on the sadistic.

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:06.960
For instance, when he first had to bulk up
for Green Lantern, the actor worked out seven

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.610
days a week, 90 minutes a day, and never did
the same workout twice — for six straight

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.610
months.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.710
Even his rest days just involved a less intense
type of exercise, like Pilates.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.110
But don't worry; for those of us who aren't
putting our abs on display for an audience

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:25.060
of millions, 20 minutes of moderate exercise
daily and three gym sessions per week will

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.040
be more than adequate to keep you fit.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.290
He eats all of the food

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.409
When it comes to playing Deadpool, the first
time Reynolds suited up wasn't in his own

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:37.520
stand-alone film — it was in 2009's X-Men
Origins: Wolverine, a regrettable outing that

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.720
would eventually become the butt of Deadpool's
best marketing jokes.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.579
"But, the movie, that was a career low for
me, you understand."

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:47.380
But back then, the actor wasn't going to pass
up the chance to bring Wade Wilson to life

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:52.320
onscreen, and he had to bulk up fast — which
meant consuming enormous amounts of food.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.280
Reynolds said that he had to eat live children
in order to put on so much muscle in so little

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.810
time — but he was kidding, of course.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.810
Probably.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.310
He focuses on nutrition

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.369
The theme of any good superhero diet?

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:07.580
Protein, protein, and protein — and if you're
Ryan Reynolds, plenty of carbs, too.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.500
The actor says, "I really don't believe in
that no-carb stuff.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.950
It's probably not good for you — and it
makes you pretty cranky."

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.940
No amount of exercise will make up for poor
nutrition.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.220
Eating the right foods in the right amounts
— and at the right times, if you're being

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.520
really intense about it — is key to building
a physique like this one.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.920
That said, even superheroes get the occasional
cheat day to indulge in some not-so-healthy

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:27.920
foods like...

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.160
"It's a chimichanga"

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.910
But actually, Reynolds prefers to gorge on
pizza when he doesn't have to look ripped

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:33.950
onscreen.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.300
He keeps it tight

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.360
Ryan Reynolds might shed some muscle or change
up his workout between superhero flicks, but

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.130
he's basically been in battle-ready shape
for the past fifteen years — which makes

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.880
it easy to ramp things back up when he needs
to slide into a spandex suit.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.270
According to his longtime trainer Bobby Strom,
"For [action films] he was 200 pounds and

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.500
8 percent body fat.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.370
For rom-coms, he's about 180 and 11 percent
body fat."

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:00.560
But even then, Reynolds is a gym regular;
says Strom, "When he does a comedy, he probably

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.550
goes to the gym to do cable work every other
day."

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.620
He sets challenging goals

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.870
Reynolds has said that getting in shape for
movie roles left him astonished at what could

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.340
be achieved with a solid workout regimen — and
now, he keeps himself motivated by giving

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.420
himself new goals to strive for.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.230
Of course, for someone as fit as Reynolds,
those goals have to be pretty intense.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.950
Among the items already crossed off his bucket
list is running the New York City marathon

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.420
in under four hours.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.420
Next up?

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.150
He wants to climb Machu Picchu.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.810
He has fun with it
Ultimately, Ryan Reynolds approaches fitness

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.510
the same way he approaches… well, everything:
by not taking himself too seriously.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:39.870
Sometimes that means finding motivation in
unusual places — like a friendly rivalry

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:44.460
with his Deadpool 2 co-star Josh Brolin, who
got even more muscled up than Reynolds to

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.730
play the character Cable.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:49.810
But the actor also knows his limits, and isn't
afraid to point out when another superhero

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:52.370
star has surpassed him in physical achievement.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.730
When asked how his own regimen stacked up
against Hugh Jackman's, who would wake up

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:59.810
at two o'clock in the morning in order to
eat enough to fuel his Wolverine workouts,

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:03.790
Reynolds said, "Hugh Jackman has a dedication
to his craft that I'm afraid I don't share.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:07.040
If I'm up at 2 in the morning, it's because
something has gone terribly wrong."

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.050
That laid-back attitude keeps the actor sane,
and it doesn't hurt that it's totally in character.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.050
"Superhero landing!

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:16.720
You know, that's really hard on your knees.Totally
impractical they all do it."

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:17.730
Thanks for watching!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.530
